## Context

The user requests monthly updates. Collection already exists; the missing publication workflow must preserve old editions, expose changes and give a named release owner a repeatable procedure.

Plan: `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md`. Parent tracker: 0725.

## First test

First failing release-diff fixture: one unchanged source, one revised amount, one newly observed older event, one blocked source and one retracted claim. The new edition must classify the changes correctly and keep the prior edition reproducible; a failed retrieval must not erase a project.

## Actions

Reuse make jetp-harvest, docs/jetp-tracking.md and refresh guidance in 0722. Inventory existing release/automation capabilities before introducing any scheduler. Specify monthly calendar, owner, review cutoff, correction policy and safe publication procedure. Rehearse two editions, expose what changed and document failed-refresh handling. Respect existing DVC ownership; archive references need not redistribute raw documents.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Calendar, release owner and reviewed publication procedure documented
- [ ] Edition comparison distinguishes real events, late reports and corrections
- [ ] Two-edition rehearsal preserves old downloads and source references
- [ ] Website exposes monthly changes and release history
- [ ] Monthly routine exercised with recorded effort and unresolved coverage; no silent publication on failed validation

## Validation

Apply the repository gates for the actual diff. Code work starts with the failing
fixture above; prose/data work records the documentary acceptance check. Preserve
source evidence and report limits rather than manufacturing a successful result.

## Storage implementation contract

Use `data/jetp/editorial/editions/` and versioned descriptors under `data/jetp/releases/`. Preserve immutable downloads, distinguish late reports from new events, and review narratives affected by changed observations. No descriptor may refer to its own commit hash.

